# 基本図形編集の線色のパレットで、色の部品を押して色を選ぶ (design 11.3, 17.13), for
# tools/ui_run.py: the desktop's figure editor and the process the same. A figure of one
# rectangle and two zigzag lines (mkbig fig 1 2 0) opened at 100,100; its 道具パネル at the
# top of the screen (100,0). The rectangle template taken and a rectangle drawn (it is then
# picked); 線色 (under 162,48) brought up: its window stands at 146,70, framed with no title,
# its work area from 152,76. Its 線色 part (270,83 to 380,105) pressed: the system's panel
# of colours comes up under it with its corner at 270,107; the ready colour of the chart's
# second row, third column (345,393) pressed and Enter: the rectangle takes it, the part
# shows it, and the swatches below mark it only if one of them has it. Escape puts the
# palette away. Saved, record 0 comes out the same, byte for byte; the screens of the
# palette after the choice are kept for comparing.
# Keys: Esc 29, Enter 28; Ctrl+S 16 01, Ctrl+E 08 01.
# the desktop's figure editor opened by open, whatever the program object says (figproc kernel)
figproc kernel
mkbig fig 1 2 0
open big
waitwin 画用紙 600
sync 600
wait 500
click 298 82
wait 300
drag 450 450 600 560
wait 400
click 162 48
wait 500
shot ccmp_k_palette
click 320 94
wait 800
shot ccmp_k_pick
click 345 393
wait 300
key 28
wait 500
shot ccmp_k_chosen
key 29
wait 300
sync 600
key 16 01
sync 600
sum show
keep kernel
key 08 01
sync 600
wait 500
mkbig fig 1 2 0
logmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 3
wait 800
logmark
click 298 82
expectsince figure: tool 7
drag 450 450 600 560
expectsince figure: drawn
logmark
click 162 48
expectsince figure: palette 1 open
wait 500
shot ccmp_p_palette
click 320 94
wait 800
shot ccmp_p_pick
click 345 393
wait 300
key 28
expectsince figure: colour chosen
wait 500
shot ccmp_p_chosen
key 29
expectsince figure: palette 1 closed
wait 300
logmark
key 16 01
expectsince figure: saved (0)
sum show
same kernel
key 08 01
expect figure: closed
